WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0006: Tav's BG3 surface detail under WoW's light (on top of 0001-0005).

- wowbg3_tav.rs: per-vertex normals and tangents from BG3's qtangent frames (axes picked by the
  faces and the UV gradients; the quaternion's sign flips mirrored halves), tangents skinned on
  the CPU, triangles re-wound for the mirrored mapping; tavtex.txt's normal and surface maps
  (TVT flag 4 linear, normal mips renormalised) on a WoW model material marked TAV_SURFACE; a
  new plan keeps persisting meshes' looks and hides new meshes until their maps arrive.
  Knobs: WOW_BG3_TAV_SPEC (highlight, 0.5), WOW_BG3_TAV_NORMAL_Y=flip, WOW_BG3_TAV_MAPS=off.
- materials.rs: TAV_SURFACE_MARKER (clutter_fade.z bit 14), a WowModelKey axis that sets the
  WOW_TAV_SURFACE shader def.
- wow_model.wgsl: vertex tangents passed through (only Tav's meshes carry them); under
  WOW_TAV_SURFACE the normal-mapped normal, occlusion on the ambient term and a restrained GGX
  highlight of the sun from roughness and metalness.

